WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:42.550
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:42.820 --> 01:47.979
[When I Meet The Moon]

3
01:48.160 --> 01:50.940
[Episode 5]

4
01:54.840 --> 01:55.620
Uncle.

5
01:57.509 --> 01:59.060
Thank you too.

6
02:07.230 --> 02:09.030
Uncle, what's going on?

7
02:11.120 --> 02:11.910
No idea.

8
02:12.780 --> 02:14.020
I've fixed everything.

9
02:14.020 --> 02:14.780
I'm off.

10
02:14.780 --> 02:16.070
Aren't you staying for dinner?

11
02:16.070 --> 02:16.750
No, thanks.

12
02:22.630 --> 02:23.740
Yes!

13
02:24.240 --> 02:25.030
I finally get to

14
02:25.030 --> 02:26.250
work with you!

15
02:26.900 --> 02:28.560
Thank you, thank you.

16
02:36.360 --> 02:37.590
Hello, Mrs. Jiang.

17
02:37.800 --> 02:38.590
Shize,

18
02:38.840 --> 02:39.800
what should we do?

19
02:39.800 --> 02:40.960
Grandma is missing.

20
02:41.030 --> 02:41.750
Your uncle and I

21
02:41.750 --> 02:43.500
have been looking for her for ages, but we still haven't found her.

22
02:43.500 --> 02:44.960
Don't worry, Mrs. Jiang.

23
02:45.240 --> 02:46.300
I'll be right over.

24
02:51.310 --> 02:52.770
What's taking him so long?

25
02:52.930 --> 02:53.590
Mrs. Jiang.

26
02:54.180 --> 02:55.020
You're finally here!

27
02:55.020 --> 02:55.370
What happened?

28
02:55.370 --> 02:56.370
I'm worried sick.

29
02:56.410 --> 02:58.120
Grandma and I were at the shop this afternoon.

30
02:58.120 --> 02:59.079
I just went inside

31
02:59.079 --> 03:00.180
to take a phone call,

32
03:00.180 --> 03:01.910
and when I came back, she was gone.

33
03:01.910 --> 03:03.340
Your uncle went out looking for her,

34
03:03.340 --> 03:04.910
but I still haven't heard from him.

35
03:04.910 --> 03:06.020
What if something's happened to her?

36
03:06.020 --> 03:07.340
Should we call the police?

37
03:07.340 --> 03:08.310
Mrs. Jiang, I—

38
03:08.710 --> 03:09.310
Uncle.

39
03:09.310 --> 03:09.930
You're back.

40
03:09.930 --> 03:11.530
Where is she? Did you find her?

41
03:11.530 --> 03:13.120
No. She hasn't come back yet?

42
03:13.120 --> 03:14.180
No, not yet.

43
03:14.710 --> 03:16.500
Mrs. Jiang, please don't panic.

44
03:16.500 --> 03:17.020
I'll help

45
03:17.020 --> 03:17.870
look for her.

46
03:18.210 --> 03:19.240
Then I'll go too.

47
03:19.240 --> 03:19.579
That's enough.

48
03:19.579 --> 03:20.810
Stay home and wait.

49
03:20.910 --> 03:21.630
If she comes back,

50
03:21.630 --> 03:22.740
call me right away.

51
03:22.740 --> 03:24.740
Call me as soon as you have an update.

52
03:45.590 --> 03:46.240
Listen,

53
03:46.630 --> 03:47.470
I found this

54
03:47.470 --> 03:48.910
huge open space recently.

55
03:48.910 --> 03:49.900
It's right over there,

56
03:49.900 --> 03:51.400
perfect for playing soccer.

57
03:51.400 --> 03:52.370
I've mastered Carlos's

58
03:52.370 --> 03:53.630
free-kick technique.

59
03:53.910 --> 03:54.520
Just wait.

60
03:54.520 --> 03:56.650
I'm gonna show you what I can do in a bit.

61
04:07.280 --> 04:07.840
Take it.

62
04:08.740 --> 04:09.200
Come on.

63
04:09.500 --> 04:10.500
Get ready.

64
04:12.090 --> 04:12.810
Pass it!

65
04:13.780 --> 04:14.240
Take it.

66
04:14.710 --> 04:15.210
Pass it to me!

67
04:15.210 --> 04:15.870
Not bad.

68
04:17.480 --> 04:17.950
Yuan.

69
04:18.620 --> 04:19.240
Take it.

70
04:28.530 --> 04:30.170
Yuan, Shize,

71
04:30.450 --> 04:31.220
play a little longer,

72
04:31.220 --> 04:33.020
then we'll head back for dinner.

73
04:33.360 --> 04:34.560
Okay, be right there.

74
04:34.810 --> 04:35.810
Coming, Grandma.

75
04:58.630 --> 04:59.360
Yuan,

76
05:00.240 --> 05:00.980
Yuan,

77
05:02.810 --> 05:04.600
why are you home so late?

78
05:05.690 --> 05:06.500
Grandma.

79
05:07.250 --> 05:08.300
Did you get held up

80
05:08.300 --> 05:08.810
by all the things you had

81
05:08.810 --> 05:09.860
to do at school?

82
05:13.510 --> 05:14.420
Where's Shize?

83
05:15.300 --> 05:17.160
Did Shize get into trouble again?

84
05:19.720 --> 05:20.750
He's still young

85
05:21.600 --> 05:23.200
and doesn't know any better.

86
05:23.300 --> 05:24.560
As his elder brother,

87
05:24.620 --> 05:26.220
you need to keep an eye on him.

88
05:31.420 --> 05:32.220
Shize,

89
05:33.030 --> 05:33.690
why

90
05:33.720 --> 05:35.280
the long face?

91
05:37.300 --> 05:39.630
You were so adorable when you were little.

92
05:40.010 --> 05:41.390
You two brothers

93
05:41.620 --> 05:43.950
were always finding ways to make me laugh.

94
05:45.310 --> 05:46.170
But these days,

95
05:47.920 --> 05:49.690
I hardly ever see you smile.

96
05:51.560 --> 05:53.000
Kids who smile a lot

97
05:54.420 --> 05:56.060
have good luck,

98
05:56.670 --> 05:58.960
so remember to smile more often.

99
06:08.100 --> 06:08.830
Grandma,

100
06:10.370 --> 06:12.100
let's go. I'll take you home.

101
06:12.660 --> 06:13.240
Okay.

102
06:31.600 --> 06:33.600
I'm gonna be late! I'm gonna be late!

103
06:39.360 --> 06:40.490
I can't run anymore.

104
06:40.510 --> 06:41.970
Make way! Coming through!

105
06:42.120 --> 06:43.750
Make way, make way, make way!

106
06:48.000 --> 06:49.800
Aren't you usually glued to your skateboard?

107
06:49.800 --> 06:51.730
Finally decided to get your feet on the ground today?

108
06:51.730 --> 06:52.659
My skateboard broke.

109
06:52.659 --> 06:53.510
I snapped it

110
06:53.510 --> 06:54.510
during practice yesterday.

111
06:54.510 --> 06:55.420
Who knows when the new one

112
06:55.420 --> 06:56.680
I ordered will arrive?

113
06:57.070 --> 06:57.770
Hop on.

114
07:01.300 --> 07:02.100
Hop on what?

115
07:02.250 --> 07:03.220
I'm...

116
07:03.510 --> 07:05.710
I'm getting some exercise, that's all.

117
07:05.810 --> 07:07.620
Trying to save face, huh?

118
07:08.100 --> 07:08.770
You'll lose points

119
07:08.770 --> 07:09.630
if you're late.

120
07:11.010 --> 07:11.770
Then again,

121
07:11.810 --> 07:13.540
what do I care?

122
07:13.540 --> 07:15.670
It's not my points they're deducting.

123
07:17.310 --> 07:18.420
Well, it's just...

124
07:19.070 --> 07:20.670
there's no seat on your bike.

125
07:20.810 --> 07:22.340
How am I supposed to ride it?

126
07:32.510 --> 07:33.720
Isn't that Fu Zhengchu?

127
07:33.720 --> 07:34.430
Why is Fu Zhengchu

128
07:34.430 --> 07:35.620
riding on the back of a girl's bike?

129
07:35.620 --> 07:36.480
Senior Fu?

130
07:36.510 --> 07:38.440
What's going on between those two?

131
07:51.480 --> 07:53.409
When's your skateboard arriving?

132
07:53.870 --> 07:55.270
Sometime later.

133
07:55.270 --> 07:56.220
Why do you ask?

134
07:56.860 --> 07:57.570
No reason.

135
07:57.630 --> 07:59.360
Let's add each other on WeChat.

136
07:59.570 --> 08:00.630
WeChat?

137
08:01.540 --> 08:03.330
I could help you if you ever need anything.

138
08:03.330 --> 08:04.070
I'm running late for class.

139
08:04.070 --> 08:05.000
Maybe next time.

140
08:08.270 --> 08:09.730
Trying so hard to act cool.

141
08:17.380 --> 08:17.950
Hello.

142
08:18.130 --> 08:18.690
Hello.

143
08:25.750 --> 08:26.620
Yes, yes,

144
08:27.220 --> 08:28.000
they said

145
08:28.000 --> 08:30.330
they won't have it ready until Wednesday.

146
08:42.270 --> 08:42.909
Excuse me,

147
08:42.909 --> 08:43.929
sorry to bother you.

148
08:43.929 --> 08:45.830
I'm the new intern.

149
08:45.910 --> 08:47.120
I wanted to ask

150
08:47.120 --> 08:47.790
who's in charge of coordinating—

151
08:47.790 --> 08:48.410
Yun Li!

152
08:50.620 --> 08:51.820
It's fine, thank you.

153
08:53.620 --> 08:54.290
Jiameng.

154
08:54.700 --> 08:55.430
You're here.

155
08:55.620 --> 08:56.770
I'll show you to your desk.

156
08:56.770 --> 08:57.340
Okay.

157
08:57.340 --> 08:57.870
Let's go.

158
09:00.580 --> 09:01.820
There are so few openings

159
09:01.820 --> 09:02.940
in the Engineering Department this year,

160
09:02.940 --> 09:04.010
and the competition is fierce.

161
09:04.010 --> 09:05.120
There wasn't much choice.

162
09:05.120 --> 09:06.670
Luckily, you were willing to join the publicity department.

163
09:06.670 --> 09:08.010
I didn't think too much about it.

164
09:08.010 --> 09:09.000
I'm just happy

165
09:09.000 --> 09:10.120
to be at EAW.

166
09:10.240 --> 09:11.370
By the way, Jiameng,

167
09:11.590 --> 09:13.790
what does the publicity department do?

168
09:14.240 --> 09:15.870
Our company was only established recently,

169
09:15.870 --> 09:16.370
and everything

170
09:16.370 --> 09:17.900
is still growing steadily.

171
09:18.630 --> 09:19.700
EAW's

172
09:19.700 --> 09:20.170
KPIs

173
09:20.170 --> 09:20.840
rely heavily on the support

174
09:20.840 --> 09:22.500
of the publicity department.

175
09:22.530 --> 09:23.580
So what will

176
09:23.580 --> 09:25.120
my main responsibilities be?

177
09:25.120 --> 09:26.170
That depends on

178
09:26.170 --> 09:27.030
what your department

179
09:27.030 --> 09:28.030
needs.

180
09:28.120 --> 09:29.720
Just do your best to help out.

181
09:29.840 --> 09:30.580
You might even

182
09:30.580 --> 09:32.840
have to lend a hand to other departments.

183
09:33.340 --> 09:36.070
So basically, I'm running errands for everyone.

184
09:37.000 --> 09:38.270
Well, coordination and teamwork

185
09:38.270 --> 09:39.890
are important, too.

186
09:40.860 --> 09:41.860
Here's your desk.

187
09:42.290 --> 09:42.890
Okay.

188
09:42.940 --> 09:43.980
Ms. Fang is still busy.

189
09:43.980 --> 09:45.100
Take some time to get familiar with things first.

190
09:45.100 --> 09:45.580
All right.

191
09:45.580 --> 09:46.100
If you need anything,

192
09:46.100 --> 09:47.830
feel free to come to me anytime.

193
09:50.670 --> 09:51.270
Hi, everyone.

194
09:51.270 --> 09:51.840
Hey!

195
09:51.840 --> 09:52.600
What's your name?

196
09:52.600 --> 09:53.250
Yun Li.

197
09:59.980 --> 10:00.770
Lili,

198
10:00.940 --> 10:02.370
let's go have some fun after work

199
10:02.370 --> 10:03.220
to celebrate

200
10:03.220 --> 10:04.080
your first day!

201
10:04.940 --> 10:05.620
Sure.

202
10:10.030 --> 10:11.290
See you after work.

203
10:12.740 --> 10:14.600
Isn't that the girl from earlier?

204
10:15.630 --> 10:16.440
Hello,

205
10:16.530 --> 10:17.940
I'm Yunli, the new intern

206
10:17.940 --> 10:18.940
starting today.

207
10:19.580 --> 10:21.100
I look forward to learning from you all.

208
10:21.100 --> 10:22.870
Please let me know if there's anything I can help with.

209
10:22.870 --> 10:23.440
Alright,

210
10:24.100 --> 10:25.500
go make me a cup of coffee.

211
10:28.530 --> 10:29.100
Excuse me.

212
10:29.100 --> 10:30.230
Here's your coffee.

213
10:34.980 --> 10:36.440
Are you trying to scald me?

214
10:36.860 --> 10:37.320
I'm sorry.

215
10:37.320 --> 10:38.430
I'll make you another cup.

216
10:38.430 --> 10:39.390
Forget it, forget it.

217
10:39.390 --> 10:41.720
You can't even make a decent cup of coffee.

218
10:41.820 --> 10:42.750
Go make 50 copies

219
10:42.810 --> 10:44.000
of these documents.

220
10:45.240 --> 10:46.030
Okay.

221
10:47.030 --> 10:47.840
I'm sorry.

222
10:51.320 --> 10:52.130
Mr. Qin,

223
10:54.320 --> 10:55.650
where's the new intern?

224
10:55.980 --> 10:56.980
Right over there.

225
10:57.010 --> 10:57.940
She's so clumsy.

226
11:00.870 --> 11:01.650
Yun Li.

227
11:03.480 --> 11:04.030
Ms. Fang.

228
11:04.030 --> 11:04.770
The engineering department

229
11:04.770 --> 11:06.440
needs extra hands for equipment maintenance today.

230
11:06.440 --> 11:07.950
Can you go help out with them?

231
11:07.950 --> 11:08.760
Ms. Fang,

232
11:09.090 --> 11:11.220
I've still got a pile of work to do here.

233
11:13.260 --> 11:14.070
Hey, you.

234
11:14.220 --> 11:15.370
Go help them,

235
11:15.620 --> 11:17.880
and come straight back when you're done.

236
11:18.440 --> 11:19.130
Okay.

237
11:31.080 --> 11:31.870
Feifei,

238
11:32.630 --> 11:34.440
why don't you come in to work today?

239
11:34.440 --> 11:35.700
I can't, Mr. Qin.

240
11:35.730 --> 11:37.260
I've got things to do today.

241
11:37.630 --> 11:40.230
If you don't show up soon, you'll lose this job.

242
11:54.620 --> 11:55.410
You're here.

243
12:04.050 --> 12:04.840
Thank you.

244
12:06.820 --> 12:07.620
I mean,

245
12:09.250 --> 12:10.840
thank you for suggesting

246
12:10.840 --> 12:11.750
EAW

247
12:17.360 --> 12:19.150
Ms. Fang asked me to come help you.

248
12:19.150 --> 12:20.610
Is there anything I can do?

249
12:23.100 --> 12:24.360
No need to be so formal.

250
12:30.270 --> 12:30.870
Let's go.

251
12:41.620 --> 12:42.420
Screwdriver.

252
12:48.890 --> 12:50.860
Did you skip breakfast?

253
12:51.600 --> 12:54.000
I noticed you only had a cup of coffee on your desk.

254
12:54.000 --> 12:56.500
Do you usually just have coffee for breakfast?

255
12:56.500 --> 12:57.000
Yeah.

256
12:58.150 --> 12:59.440
Just having coffee for breakfast

257
12:59.440 --> 13:01.040
isn't good for your stomach.

258
13:02.940 --> 13:05.460
You said last time that you liked crepe rolls.

259
13:05.460 --> 13:07.550
How about I make some and bring them for you?

260
13:07.550 --> 13:08.360
No need.

261
13:12.050 --> 13:12.890
I heard

262
13:13.200 --> 13:14.200
you've competed in

263
13:14.200 --> 13:15.750
lots of robotics competitions.

264
13:15.750 --> 13:17.350
You must be really good at it.

265
13:17.600 --> 13:18.390
I'm not bad.

266
13:19.890 --> 13:20.700
Actually,

267
13:21.220 --> 13:22.960
I love robots too.

268
13:23.680 --> 13:25.210
I've even built one myself.

269
13:31.170 --> 13:32.200
Do you think it's weird

270
13:32.200 --> 13:34.270
that I'm into robots?

271
13:36.840 --> 13:37.290
No.

272
13:40.000 --> 13:41.460
Building a robot yourself

273
13:43.840 --> 13:44.700
is impressive.

274
13:46.390 --> 13:47.520
You really think so?

275
14:02.580 --> 14:03.890
What should we do next?

276
14:05.440 --> 14:06.640
What do you want to do?

277
14:06.870 --> 14:08.390
That's a funny question.

278
14:08.670 --> 14:10.400
Shouldn't I be asking you that?

279
14:15.580 --> 14:17.100
This looks like one of those

280
14:17.100 --> 14:18.480
old arcade games.

281
14:19.440 --> 14:20.840
Did you play them as a kid?

282
14:22.170 --> 14:22.980
No.

283
14:23.790 --> 14:25.450
Then what did you play as a kid?

284
14:27.670 --> 14:29.270
I used to play with my nephew.

285
14:30.670 --> 14:32.740
What did you play with Fu Zhengchu?

286
14:33.440 --> 14:34.770
He liked playing house.

287
14:47.100 --> 14:47.720
Come here.

288
15:20.240 --> 15:22.100
Should I tighten it a little more?

289
15:31.860 --> 15:32.580
Too tight?

290
15:35.510 --> 15:36.480
A little.

291
15:49.270 --> 15:49.930
Your hands.

292
16:13.910 --> 16:14.740
Pick a mode.

293
16:17.080 --> 16:17.670
This game

294
16:17.670 --> 16:18.930
requires two players.

295
16:20.230 --> 16:21.940
Please select a game mode.

296
16:21.960 --> 16:23.670
A. Parent-Child Mode

297
16:24.250 --> 16:24.960
Parent-child mode.

298
16:24.960 --> 16:26.190
B. Couple Mode

299
16:26.600 --> 16:28.320
I think this Parent-child mode

300
16:28.320 --> 16:29.480
describes our relationship

301
16:29.480 --> 16:30.370
best.

302
16:31.220 --> 16:32.080
You can be the dad,

303
16:32.080 --> 16:33.480
and I can be the daughter.

304
16:34.340 --> 16:36.370
Or I can be the mom,

305
16:36.370 --> 16:37.370
and you can be the—

306
16:41.010 --> 16:41.670
Never mind.

307
17:01.620 --> 17:03.080
The game is about to begin.

308
17:03.170 --> 17:04.440
Please get ready.

309
17:06.000 --> 17:06.420
Daddy,

310
17:06.440 --> 17:08.720
are you taking me on an adventure in the woods?

311
17:08.720 --> 17:10.349
That's right. Let's go!

312
17:20.060 --> 17:20.750
[Caution: obstacle ahead]

313
17:21.510 --> 17:22.140
[Swerve left]

314
17:27.200 --> 17:28.010
[Swerve left]

315
17:29.530 --> 17:31.330
Hold on tight, kiddo.

316
17:30.860 --> 17:31.540
[Swerve right]

317
17:31.550 --> 17:32.680
Don't fall off!

318
17:46.210 --> 17:46.810
[Multiple obstacles ahead! Watch out!]

319
17:51.470 --> 17:52.390
[Swerve left. Obstacle ahead!]

320
17:56.680 --> 17:57.720
[Swerve right. Obstacle ahead!]

321
18:00.130 --> 18:01.360
[Swerve left. Obstacle ahead!]

322
18:02.680 --> 18:03.840
[Swerve right. Obstacle ahead!]

323
18:13.840 --> 18:14.460
[Swerve left. Obstacle ahead!]

324
18:34.350 --> 18:36.410
We're about to reach the finish line.

325
18:51.850 --> 18:52.660
Was it fun?

326
18:55.930 --> 18:58.520
This mode is a little unusual.

327
18:59.350 --> 19:00.010
Unusual?

328
19:00.960 --> 19:02.750
M-Maybe it's because we were in Parent-Child Mode.

329
19:02.750 --> 19:03.700
It probably leaves out some

330
19:03.700 --> 19:05.560
of the shooting actions for kids.

331
19:09.160 --> 19:10.960
So you didn't get to do anything.

332
19:12.510 --> 19:13.310
Yeah.

333
19:14.360 --> 19:16.010
Maybe that's just

334
19:16.010 --> 19:16.790
how Parent-Child Mode works.

335
19:16.790 --> 19:19.050
The kid just sits in the back

336
19:19.330 --> 19:20.660
and enjoys the scenery.

337
19:21.750 --> 19:22.550
Was it nice?

338
19:24.170 --> 19:25.610
It was pretty nice.

339
19:33.200 --> 19:34.260
Good morning, sir.

340
19:35.350 --> 19:36.500
Look at you, young lady.

341
19:36.500 --> 19:38.100
You're positively beaming.

342
19:38.220 --> 19:39.900
What's got you in such a good mood?

343
19:39.900 --> 19:41.420
I'm the new intern,

344
19:41.420 --> 19:42.200
Yun Li.

345
19:42.200 --> 19:43.420
Have a wonderful day!

346
19:43.420 --> 19:44.620
All right, all right.

347
19:47.850 --> 19:49.910
Good things put a spring in your step.

348
19:50.400 --> 19:52.070
Ah, to be young again!

349
20:30.720 --> 20:31.160
Yuan.

350
20:35.200 --> 20:36.160
Go by yourself.

351
20:36.590 --> 20:37.400
Come on, Yuan.

352
20:37.630 --> 20:38.270
Help me out.

353
20:38.270 --> 20:39.040
I don't want to.

354
20:39.040 --> 20:39.870
What are you doing?

355
20:39.870 --> 20:40.800
You're the best.

356
20:50.830 --> 20:51.640
Excuse me.

357
20:52.000 --> 20:53.130
Sorry to bother you.

358
20:55.640 --> 20:57.310
M-My friend and I

359
21:01.240 --> 21:02.000
were over there watching

360
21:02.000 --> 21:03.160
you play with this robot

361
21:03.160 --> 21:04.160
for quite a while.

362
21:05.240 --> 21:06.570
I'm not playing with it.

363
21:06.590 --> 21:07.790
I'm training it.

364
21:10.720 --> 21:12.400
This robot is pretty cute.

365
21:13.310 --> 21:14.770
Did you build it yourself?

366
21:15.240 --> 21:15.770
Yeah.

367
21:20.070 --> 21:21.510
Why don't you try this?

368
21:26.960 --> 21:28.160
I'll get going, then.

369
21:31.240 --> 21:31.920
All delivered.

370
21:31.920 --> 21:32.590
Come on, let's go.

371
21:32.590 --> 21:33.550
Aren't you going to say something to her?

372
21:33.550 --> 21:34.410
No, no.

373
21:34.440 --> 21:35.440
Come on, let's go.

374
22:07.660 --> 22:09.350
Isn't coffee his favorite?

375
22:09.660 --> 22:11.460
How come he hasn't even had a sip?

376
22:38.500 --> 22:39.160
Here you go.

377
22:41.240 --> 22:42.230
Thanks.

378
22:43.750 --> 22:44.510
Didn't we agree

379
22:44.510 --> 22:45.240
to go have some fun?

380
22:45.240 --> 22:46.970
How come we're back here again?

381
22:48.700 --> 22:51.430
Look at that smile! You're practically glowing.

382
22:51.740 --> 22:52.600
Come on, spill.

383
22:52.850 --> 22:54.090
First day at work,

384
22:54.140 --> 22:55.160
and did things with your dream guy

385
22:55.160 --> 22:56.250
go better

386
22:56.500 --> 22:58.500
than expected?

387
22:58.790 --> 23:00.240
It's not that dramatic.

388
23:00.440 --> 23:01.700
We just got a little closer

389
23:01.700 --> 23:04.330
because of work.

390
23:05.160 --> 23:06.160
Just getting a tiny bit closer

391
23:06.160 --> 23:07.500
has you this excited?

392
23:08.750 --> 23:10.440
You're such a lovesick fool.

393
23:13.400 --> 23:14.740
Honestly, Xia's uncle seems

394
23:14.740 --> 23:16.530
to really look out for you.

395
23:16.660 --> 23:18.720
Maybe you two actually have a chance.

396
23:19.660 --> 23:20.530
I think so, too.

397
23:20.640 --> 23:22.370
He's really considerate of me.

398
23:26.720 --> 23:28.590
Uncle treats all of us younger-generation relatives so well.

399
23:28.590 --> 23:30.030
Whenever we went out,

400
23:30.030 --> 23:30.590
he was always the one

401
23:30.590 --> 23:32.240
who'd wait in line and pay for everything.

402
23:32.240 --> 23:33.660
When my sister and I were little,

403
23:33.660 --> 23:34.720
all we had to do was call out "Uncle,"

404
23:34.720 --> 23:36.520
and we had everything we needed.

405
23:36.640 --> 23:38.170
The younger generation...

406
23:38.400 --> 23:39.800
The younger generation!

407
23:39.830 --> 23:40.440
Tangy,

408
23:40.900 --> 23:42.350
what if Fu Shize really sees me

409
23:42.350 --> 23:44.610
as someone from the younger generation?

410
23:44.750 --> 23:45.850
What do you mean, the younger generation?

411
23:45.850 --> 23:47.380
Aren't you two the same age?

412
23:48.290 --> 23:49.660
He skipped the rest of elementary school

413
23:49.660 --> 23:51.140
and went straight to junior high.

414
23:51.140 --> 23:52.350
So he's been surrounded by people

415
23:52.350 --> 23:54.240
older than him since he was little.

416
23:54.240 --> 23:55.850
He probably never even realized

417
23:55.850 --> 23:57.440
we're the same age.

418
23:58.200 --> 23:59.240
Plus, he became an uncle

419
23:59.240 --> 24:00.200
at such a young age,

420
24:00.200 --> 24:01.530
and he's always around his nephews

421
24:01.530 --> 24:02.750
and nieces.

422
24:02.850 --> 24:04.090
And since I hang out with Fu Zhengchu

423
24:04.090 --> 24:04.960
and the others,

424
24:05.200 --> 24:06.750
what if he really sees me as one of the younger generation?

425
24:06.750 --> 24:08.350
What am I supposed to do then?

426
24:08.900 --> 24:09.530
I mean,

427
24:09.530 --> 24:10.900
it's not impossible.

428
24:11.330 --> 24:13.350
You're supposed to be his girlfriend,

429
24:13.350 --> 24:14.350
so don't let some twist of fate

430
24:14.350 --> 24:16.150
turn you into his niece instead.

431
24:18.090 --> 24:19.250
Why do I feel like

432
24:20.010 --> 24:21.220
I'm getting further and further

433
24:21.220 --> 24:23.220
down the path to becoming his niece?

434
24:24.290 --> 24:25.010
Then we need to find a way

435
24:25.010 --> 24:26.270
to turn things around.

436
24:26.510 --> 24:27.310
How?

437
24:27.810 --> 24:28.610
Well...

438
24:29.810 --> 24:31.590
ask him how old he is,

439
24:31.590 --> 24:32.510
then tell him

440
24:32.510 --> 24:33.610
your birthday.

441
24:33.610 --> 24:34.350
That way, he'll realize

442
24:34.350 --> 24:35.480
you're the same age.

443
24:37.980 --> 24:39.440
Do you think that'll work?

444
24:39.590 --> 24:41.380
Whether it works or not, you have to try.

445
24:41.380 --> 24:42.700
Do you really want to end up with another uncle?

446
24:42.700 --> 24:43.440
No way.

447
25:02.970 --> 25:05.360
[Robot Soccer Tournament]

448
25:06.590 --> 25:09.790
[XUST Football Field]

449
25:09.810 --> 25:11.590
[Specially invited by the tournament: XUST Unique team members as team leaders.]

450
25:30.710 --> 25:31.710
Hey, Li.

451
25:31.740 --> 25:32.800
What are you doing?

452
25:33.030 --> 25:33.960
Studying.

453
25:34.500 --> 25:35.590
Go to my room now

454
25:35.620 --> 25:37.010
and video call me.

455
25:46.660 --> 25:48.480
Yun Li, I'm in.

456
25:48.850 --> 25:50.580
See that wardrobe on the right?

457
25:50.960 --> 25:51.920
There's a box on top.

458
25:51.920 --> 25:52.660
Do you see it?

459
25:52.680 --> 25:53.480
This one?

460
25:54.330 --> 25:55.860
Yeah, yeah, that's the one.

461
25:58.330 --> 25:59.020
Wait, Yun Li,

462
25:59.020 --> 26:00.180
what's this about?

463
26:00.400 --> 26:01.740
What do you mean?

464
26:01.850 --> 26:02.950
[Open this and you're a loser]

465
26:02.290 --> 26:03.050
Just look.

466
26:03.330 --> 26:04.160
Don't worry about that. Just open it first.

467
26:04.160 --> 26:05.150
Open it first.

468
26:08.410 --> 26:09.550
See that little robot

469
26:09.550 --> 26:11.480
I used in the competition?

470
26:13.100 --> 26:13.970
This one?

471
26:14.100 --> 26:15.330
Yeah, that's the one.

472
26:15.960 --> 26:17.400
You still have this junk?

473
26:18.570 --> 26:19.000
Wait,

474
26:19.240 --> 26:19.830
check if there's

475
26:19.830 --> 26:21.490
a blue envelope in there, too.

476
26:23.350 --> 26:23.940
This one?

477
26:23.940 --> 26:25.140
Yeah, that's the one.

478
26:25.400 --> 26:27.240
There's also a little soccer ball.

479
26:27.240 --> 26:28.840
It should be right next to it.

480
26:31.350 --> 26:32.700
Ship all of these to me.

481
26:33.040 --> 26:33.700
Gotta go.

482
26:33.750 --> 26:34.550
Wait,

483
26:36.740 --> 26:38.070
send me 200 yuan please.

484
26:38.350 --> 26:39.350
I already sent you money last time.

485
26:39.350 --> 26:40.050
No way.

486
26:56.270 --> 26:56.740
Yuan,

487
26:56.850 --> 26:57.960
I ordered this just for you.

488
26:57.960 --> 26:58.690
Give it a try.

489
26:59.290 --> 27:01.350
All right, what do you want this time?

490
27:01.670 --> 27:03.110
Yuan, here's the thing.

491
27:03.480 --> 27:04.680
My friends and I are planning

492
27:04.680 --> 27:06.220
to make a little investment.

493
27:06.220 --> 27:07.510
We're just a little short on funds.

494
27:07.510 --> 27:07.940
So, I was wondering if you could...

495
27:07.940 --> 27:08.480
Are any of your friends

496
27:08.480 --> 27:09.570
even trustworthy?

497
27:09.570 --> 27:10.310
Of course!

498
27:10.310 --> 27:11.530
Totally trustworthy.

499
27:11.530 --> 27:12.420
Our investment

500
27:12.420 --> 27:14.880
is fair, reasonable, and completely legal.

501
27:14.920 --> 27:16.270
Your mom already talked to me.

502
27:16.270 --> 27:17.420
She told me not to give you any money.

503
27:17.420 --> 27:19.020
If you need money, go ask her.

504
27:19.290 --> 27:20.110
Yuan, I just—

505
27:20.140 --> 27:21.080
Don't touch me.

506
27:21.720 --> 27:22.920
Come on, do me a favor.

507
27:23.830 --> 27:25.030
No way. That's final.

508
27:29.940 --> 27:30.510
Yuan.

509
27:30.510 --> 27:31.880
I-I'll get going, then.

510
27:35.010 --> 27:35.610
Shize.

511
27:38.110 --> 27:39.270
How did I end up

512
27:39.270 --> 27:40.530
with a cousin like him?

513
27:43.380 --> 27:44.610
You dragged me out

514
27:45.140 --> 27:47.070
in the middle of the night. What is it?

515
27:47.070 --> 27:49.070
Can't I call you out just to hang out?

516
27:49.610 --> 27:50.810
What are you drinking?

517
27:50.810 --> 27:51.530
Whiskey?

518
27:52.330 --> 27:53.830
No, I drove here.

519
27:54.030 --> 27:55.360
Get him a glass of juice.

520
28:02.440 --> 28:03.330
The Light Chaser has almost

521
28:03.330 --> 28:04.270
finished testing.

522
28:04.270 --> 28:06.640
A few more adjustments, and it'll be ready to launch.

523
28:06.640 --> 28:08.170
I didn't ask you about that.

524
28:09.810 --> 28:10.740
Isn't that

525
28:10.920 --> 28:12.050
why you asked me out?

526
28:12.810 --> 28:13.810
Can't I just

527
28:13.810 --> 28:14.240
want to have a drink with you,

528
28:14.240 --> 28:15.840
without talking about work?

529
28:19.810 --> 28:21.140
You could've done that at home.

530
28:21.140 --> 28:21.830
You've been

531
28:21.830 --> 28:22.680
so busy at the company lately.

532
28:22.680 --> 28:24.940
When would you have time to drink at home?

533
28:25.180 --> 28:25.980
How funny.

534
28:29.140 --> 28:29.900
How's your digital twin

535
28:29.900 --> 28:30.830
coming along?

536
28:32.470 --> 28:33.270
What?

537
28:34.000 --> 28:35.000
Why so secretive?

538
28:35.140 --> 28:36.400
You can't even tell me?

539
28:37.350 --> 28:38.500
You wouldn't understand even if I told you.

540
28:38.500 --> 28:39.070
You haven't even told me.

541
28:39.070 --> 28:40.700
How do you know I wouldn't understand?

542
28:40.700 --> 28:41.700
Have you forgotten

543
28:41.700 --> 28:43.140
how you and Jiang Yuan

544
28:43.140 --> 28:44.140
came to me back then

545
28:44.140 --> 28:45.070
to ask about two research areas:

546
28:45.070 --> 28:46.070
artificial intelligence (AI)

547
28:46.070 --> 28:47.590
and intelligent automation?

548
28:47.590 --> 28:48.270
I even went

549
28:48.270 --> 28:49.440
and studied

550
28:49.440 --> 28:50.680
the differences between them because of you.

551
28:50.680 --> 28:52.210
How could I not understand?

552
29:00.640 --> 29:01.440
By the way,

553
29:01.440 --> 29:02.030
isn't Great-Aunt's birthday

554
29:02.030 --> 29:03.380
coming up soon?

555
29:04.420 --> 29:05.180
You hardly ever

556
29:05.180 --> 29:06.440
get to see each other,

557
29:06.480 --> 29:07.310
so you should make a good impression

558
29:07.310 --> 29:08.810
while you have the chance.

559
29:10.380 --> 29:11.050
Got it.

560
30:57.460 --> 30:58.180
I...

561
31:25.290 --> 31:25.900
Hello.

562
31:26.920 --> 31:27.660
Who is it?

563
31:34.620 --> 31:35.990
This is my seat.

564
31:37.640 --> 31:38.740
Ms. Idle Cloud,

565
31:39.480 --> 31:40.200
they said

566
31:40.200 --> 31:41.140
our internship schedules

567
31:41.140 --> 31:42.090
are different,

568
31:42.180 --> 31:43.830
so whoever's here for work can sit here.

569
31:43.830 --> 31:45.900
What if our shifts overlap?

570
31:48.700 --> 31:50.500
Mr. Qin said you're nice

571
31:50.830 --> 31:52.760
and wouldn't fight me for the seat.

572
31:53.880 --> 31:54.680
Oh,

573
31:55.500 --> 31:57.240
and I haven't touched your stuff,

574
31:57.240 --> 31:58.040
so don't touch

575
31:58.090 --> 31:59.240
mine either.

576
32:01.200 --> 32:03.060
You sure like to play by the rules.

577
32:03.330 --> 32:04.140
Yeah.

578
32:06.940 --> 32:09.140
I thought you interviewed

579
32:09.140 --> 32:11.380
for an internship in the engineering department.

580
32:11.380 --> 32:13.840
Why are you in the publicity department too?

581
32:13.940 --> 32:15.070
Didn't make the cut?

582
32:18.000 --> 32:19.270
Don't be too upset.

583
32:19.900 --> 32:21.830
We're all just working for a living, after all.

584
32:21.830 --> 32:23.400
If you don't have what it takes,

585
32:23.400 --> 32:25.460
you shouldn't be in this line of work.

586
32:27.110 --> 32:28.310
Feifei, you're here.

587
32:29.420 --> 32:30.290
Mr. Qin.

588
32:32.140 --> 32:32.750
Yun Li,

589
32:32.750 --> 32:34.010
I forgot to tell you.

590
32:34.220 --> 32:34.980
Feifei

591
32:35.010 --> 32:36.290
is interning here too.

592
32:36.770 --> 32:38.030
I think today is the only day

593
32:38.030 --> 32:39.550
you'll be working the same shift.

594
32:39.550 --> 32:40.310
There's also

595
32:40.310 --> 32:41.500
seating in the break area,

596
32:41.500 --> 32:44.160
so you two can figure out how to divide things up.

597
32:44.350 --> 32:45.290
Mr. Qin,

598
32:45.960 --> 32:47.290
Yun Li is nice.

599
32:47.750 --> 32:49.480
You won't fight me for the seat,

600
32:49.500 --> 32:50.550
will you, Yun Li?

601
32:52.110 --> 32:53.110
Actually, I will.

602
32:53.750 --> 32:54.660
This is my seat.

603
32:54.660 --> 32:56.390
I'd appreciate it if you moved.

604
33:00.310 --> 33:01.010
Yun Li...

605
33:01.010 --> 33:01.590
Ms. Fang assigned

606
33:01.590 --> 33:02.720
this seat to me.

607
33:02.750 --> 33:04.010
If there's going to be any change in seating arrangements,

608
33:04.010 --> 33:06.270
please have Ms. Fang inform me directly.

609
33:07.250 --> 33:08.050
Feifei,

610
33:08.460 --> 33:10.310
I can't believe this new intern

611
33:10.600 --> 33:12.060
is being so unreasonable.

612
33:12.610 --> 33:14.140
I'll find you another seat.

613
33:20.110 --> 33:21.250
Pick up your things,

614
33:23.430 --> 33:24.280
new intern.

615
33:37.720 --> 33:38.510
Yun Li,

616
33:38.980 --> 33:40.040
you did great.

617
33:40.060 --> 33:42.110
You did the right thing.

618
33:52.160 --> 33:53.720
Why do people

619
33:53.720 --> 33:55.250
keep throwing their weight

620
33:55.250 --> 33:57.700
around in this office?

621
33:58.590 --> 34:00.050
That little girl was the one

622
34:00.050 --> 34:01.290
who got there first

623
34:01.290 --> 34:02.090
and took the seat.

624
34:02.090 --> 34:03.960
Why try to take it from her?

625
34:04.700 --> 34:08.230
Don't they understand the concept of first come, first served?

626
35:05.900 --> 35:06.900
Your cup's full.

627
35:11.900 --> 35:13.550
I'll get a tissue.

628
35:34.610 --> 35:35.420
You...

629
35:35.670 --> 35:37.760
This coffee smells really good.

630
35:38.960 --> 35:39.760
Want some?

631
35:41.000 --> 35:41.530
Yeah.

632
35:46.780 --> 35:47.610
Sugar?

633
35:51.170 --> 35:52.970
Do you like sugar in your coffee?

634
35:53.280 --> 35:53.980
No.

635
35:54.820 --> 35:56.010
Then I don't either.

636
35:58.360 --> 35:59.670
I really don't.

637
36:05.480 --> 36:06.110
Thanks.

638
36:14.550 --> 36:15.600
How can anyone

639
36:15.630 --> 36:17.760
drink something that tastes this bad?

640
36:22.860 --> 36:23.650
I-I...

641
36:23.650 --> 36:25.860
I think I'll add some sugar after all.

642
36:29.030 --> 36:30.230
"Then I don't either.

643
36:31.590 --> 36:32.780
I really don't."

644
36:36.010 --> 36:36.610
I...

645
36:48.000 --> 36:49.130
Go ahead if you want.

646
36:54.880 --> 36:56.480
I just want to see

647
36:56.480 --> 36:58.380
what this different-flavored coffee

648
36:58.380 --> 36:59.530
tastes like.

649
37:26.840 --> 37:27.630
Yun Li.

650
37:29.320 --> 37:29.920
Come here.

651
37:32.800 --> 37:33.690
Mr. Qin,

652
37:33.690 --> 37:34.780
what is it?

653
37:35.780 --> 37:36.780
I'm going to meet a client

654
37:36.780 --> 37:37.800
with Feifei later.

655
37:37.800 --> 37:38.590
You

656
37:38.780 --> 37:40.380
move all of this over there

657
37:40.570 --> 37:42.100
and get it done before noon.

658
37:42.630 --> 37:44.050
Before noon?

659
37:44.050 --> 37:45.800
How is that even possible?

660
37:46.000 --> 37:47.630
There's so much stuff.

661
37:47.630 --> 37:48.880
There's no way I'll finish by noon.

662
37:48.880 --> 37:50.540
Then finish it before you eat.

663
37:50.690 --> 37:51.730
Work comes first.

664
37:53.420 --> 37:54.420
Let's go, Feifei.

665
37:59.000 --> 37:59.980
This intern's going

666
37:59.980 --> 38:01.640
to have a hard time from now on.

667
38:01.780 --> 38:03.110
She crossed Qin Haigou,

668
38:03.110 --> 38:04.970
so she's in for a world of trouble.

669
38:20.440 --> 38:21.480
Aren't you going to lunch, Yun Li?

670
38:21.480 --> 38:22.920
The boxed meals will be gone soon.

671
38:22.920 --> 38:23.970
It's fine. I'm almost done.

672
38:23.970 --> 38:24.690
Go ahead.

673
38:24.690 --> 38:25.340
All right.

674
38:34.190 --> 38:35.630
Why bother?

675
38:36.130 --> 38:37.530
The food's already cold—

676
38:45.260 --> 38:46.410
Have you eaten?

677
38:47.280 --> 38:48.030
Yes.

678
38:48.300 --> 38:49.500
I've eaten too.

679
38:51.300 --> 38:53.440
So, what are you doing here?

680
38:53.880 --> 38:54.810
Getting coffee.

681
39:17.380 --> 39:19.230
H-Has he really eaten?

682
39:37.890 --> 39:38.890
Hello.

683
39:41.500 --> 39:42.460
Room 8001?

684
39:42.460 --> 39:43.010
One moment, please.

685
39:43.010 --> 39:44.130
I'll bring it to your room shortly.

686
39:44.130 --> 39:44.780
Xia,

687
39:44.780 --> 39:46.710
did your brother go to class today?

688
39:47.260 --> 39:47.940
He did.

689
39:58.820 --> 40:00.640
♪ Sitting by the window ♪

690
40:00.660 --> 40:03.010
♪ Watching the afternoon breeze ♪

691
40:03.030 --> 40:05.270
♪ Clouds like cotton candy ♪

692
40:05.300 --> 40:07.260
♪ Lining up in secret ♪

693
40:07.290 --> 40:09.420
♪ I turn my headphones up ♪

694
40:09.440 --> 40:11.420
♪ As loud as they can go ♪

695
40:11.530 --> 40:13.510
♪ Listening to my own heartbeat ♪

696
40:13.670 --> 40:15.510
♪ Something feels a little strange ♪

697
40:15.530 --> 40:16.160
Xia,

698
40:16.340 --> 40:17.870
is your brother out of class yet?

699
40:17.870 --> 40:19.930
♪ What's happening to me? ♪

700
40:19.950 --> 40:22.020
♪ I can't find the remote ♪

701
40:20.260 --> 40:21.460
How would I know?

702
40:22.050 --> 40:24.280
♪ What's happening to me now? ♪

703
40:24.310 --> 40:26.330
♪ My heart suddenly skips a beat ♪

704
40:26.350 --> 40:27.920
♪ A little anxious ♪

705
40:27.690 --> 40:28.380
Is Fu Zhengchu

706
40:27.950 --> 40:29.420
♪ A little curious ♪

707
40:28.380 --> 40:29.900
going skateboarding today, then?

708
40:29.440 --> 40:31.560
♪ My whole world is you ♪

709
40:31.590 --> 40:32.480
♪ Oh my, oh my ♪

710
40:32.510 --> 40:34.180
♪ This little craziness ♪

711
40:34.200 --> 40:36.780
♪ Feels a little sweet ♪

712
40:35.210 --> 40:36.530
Ask him yourself.

713
40:38.280 --> 40:40.190
If I could ask him in person,

714
40:40.190 --> 40:41.590
why would I be asking you?

715
40:43.170 --> 40:45.890
♪ Your little universe ♪

716
40:46.910 --> 40:48.910
♪ Will always come to you ♪

717
40:58.320 --> 41:00.280
Mr. Qin is the worst.

718
41:00.280 --> 41:01.610
He won't even let me eat!

719
41:03.940 --> 41:05.190
He never does

720
41:05.220 --> 41:06.660
a single decent thing.

721
41:11.330 --> 41:12.530
How could EAW

722
41:12.560 --> 41:14.040
hire someone like him?
